### PayX — every Payment Core scenario as a request (docs/PAYMENT-CORE.md).
#
# Visual Studio: open this file, click "Send request" above a request (or
# Ctrl+Alt+S). Run them top to bottom: later requests use earlier answers
# ({{name.response.body.$.field}}). Works the same whether a service runs in
# its container or under your debugger: see DEBUGGING.md.
#
# Every response carries X-PayX-Instance: which process answered
# (PayX.Payment@<container id> or PayX.Payment@<your PC>).
#
# Bump @run to start over with new users (usernames must be unique).

@run = 1
@gateway = http://localhost:7080
@vault = http://localhost:7084
@psp = http://localhost:7088
@password = correct horse battery

# Cards: 4242424242424242 approves. Each card number has a $5,000 limit that
# holds and captures use up; when it starts declining with insufficient_funds,
# switch to another Luhn-valid number: 4111111111111111, 4012888888881881,
# 5555555555554444, 5105105105105100.
@card = 4242424242424242


############################################################ 0. Users

### Register Priya (customer). 409 if @run was used before: bump it.
# @name registerPriya
POST {{gateway}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "priya{{run}}", "email": "priya{{run}}@example.com", "password": "{{password}}", "role": "Customer" }

### Register Shoe Shop (merchant). Its id is the merchantId in payments.
# @name registerShop
POST {{gateway}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shoeshop{{run}}", "email": "shoeshop{{run}}@example.com", "password": "{{password}}", "role": "Merchant" }

### Register Other Shop (another merchant, for the visibility checks).
# @name registerOther
POST {{gateway}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "othershop{{run}}", "email": "othershop{{run}}@example.com", "password": "{{password}}", "role": "Merchant" }

### Log in as Priya
# @name loginPriya
POST {{gateway}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "priya{{run}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Log in as Shoe Shop
# @name loginShop
POST {{gateway}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shoeshop{{run}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Log in as Other Shop
# @name loginOther
POST {{gateway}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "othershop{{run}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

@priya = {{loginPriya.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@shop = {{loginShop.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@other = {{loginOther.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@merchantId = {{registerShop.response.body.$.id}}


############################################################ §2 Checkout: tokenize the card

### Tokenize (card number + CVC go to Vault only). Breakpoint: Vault CardVault.TokenizeAsync
# @name tokenize
POST {{vault}}/api/vault/cards
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "{{card}}", "expMonth": 12, "expYear": 2030, "cvc": "123" }

@token = {{tokenize.response.body.$.token}}


############################################################ §3 Pay, approved

### Pay $50. Breakpoints: Payment IdempotencyFilter → PaymentAuthorization.AuthorizeAsync
# → Vault CardAuthorizer.AuthorizeAsync → PSP AuthorizationsController.Authorize
# @name pay
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: checkout-{{run}}-a
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 5000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{token}}" }

@paymentId = {{pay.response.body.$.id}}


############################################################ §6 Double-click: the same request again

### Same key → the same 201, header Idempotent-Replayed: true, no second payment
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: checkout-{{run}}-a
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 5000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{token}}" }


############################################################ §7 Same key, different request

### Same key, $60 instead of $50 → 422 idempotency_key_reused_with_different_request
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: checkout-{{run}}-a
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 6000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{token}}" }

### No key → 400 idempotency_key_required
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 5000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{token}}" }


############################################################ §10 Paying again with a used card token

### New key, same token: the CVC was used for the first payment → 422 cvc_unavailable
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: checkout-{{run}}-b
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 5000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{token}}" }


############################################################ §11 Status

### Priya sees her payment. Breakpoint: Payment PaymentQueries.FindVisibleAsync
GET {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

### Shoe Shop sees it too
GET {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{shop}}

### Other Shop doesn't → 404 payment_not_found
GET {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{other}}


############################################################ §13 Capture refused

### Priya (a customer) can't capture → 403
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{run}}-x

### Other Shop can't capture Shoe Shop's payment → 404
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{other}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{run}}-y

### More than authorized → 422 amount_exceeds_authorized (PSP never called)
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{shop}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{run}}-z
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amountMinor": 5001 }


############################################################ §12 Capture

### Shoe Shop captures $30 of $50. Breakpoints: Payment PaymentCapture.CaptureAsync
# → PSP AuthorizationActions (capture)
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{shop}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{run}}-a
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amountMinor": 3000 }

### Same capture, same key → the stored 200, replayed (no second capture)
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{shop}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{run}}-a
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amountMinor": 3000 }

### New key on a captured payment → 409 payment_not_capturable
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{shop}}
Idempotency-Key: capture-{{run}}-b


############################################################ §4 Declined

### Tokenize the issuer's "generic decline" test card
# @name tokenizeDecline
POST {{vault}}/api/vault/cards
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "4000000000000002", "expMonth": 12, "expYear": 2030, "cvc": "123" }

### Pay with it → 201 with status Declined, declineCode card_declined
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: checkout-{{run}}-decline
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 5000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{tokenizeDecline.response.body.$.token}}" }


############################################################ §8 Bank down during payment, then retry
#
# 1. Tokenize a fresh card (below).
# 2. docker compose stop psp-simulator   (or stop your debugger if the PSP runs in VS)
# 3. Send "Pay (PSP down)" → 502 psp_unreachable; the payment stays RiskApproved
# 4. docker compose start psp-simulator
# 5. Send "Pay (PSP down)" again, unchanged → 201 Authorized, the SAME payment id
# Breakpoints: Payment IdempotencyService.ClaimAsync (Resumed), PaymentAuthorization
# (ResumeOrCreateAsync, then straight to the Vault step), Vault CardAuthorizer (CVC kept).

### Tokenize a fresh card for this scenario
# @name tokenizeOutage
POST {{vault}}/api/vault/cards
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "{{card}}", "expMonth": 12, "expYear": 2030, "cvc": "123" }

### Pay (PSP down) — send once with the PSP stopped, then again after starting it
POST {{gateway}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Idempotency-Key: checkout-{{run}}-outage
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "{{merchantId}}", "amount": { "amountMinor": 5000, "currency": "USD" }, "cardToken": "{{tokenizeOutage.response.body.$.token}}" }


############################################################ PSP simulator directly (Phase 3)

### Authorize at the PSP directly, slowed down by X-Psp-Fault (try error=503 or timeout-after-success too)
POST {{psp}}/api/psp/authorizations
Idempotency-Key: psp-direct-{{run}}
X-Psp-Fault: latency=2000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100, "currency": "USD", "card": { "number": "{{card}}", "expMonth": 12, "expYear": 2030, "cvc": "123" }, "merchantId": "m_direct" }
